      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1785 Greeneville served as the capital of the short‑lived State of Franklin, hosting its first legislature in a log courthouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greeneville%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Niswonger Performing Arts Center stages world‑class musicians, comedians, and theater productions, keeping Greeneville’s cultural scene vibrant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
